    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "79p89in",
      "content": "Electric current is the flow of electric charge through a conductor. In electrical engineering and technical trades, two main types of electric current are used: Alternating Current (AC) and Direct Current (DC). Understanding their characteristics, applications, and differences is important for working with electrical systems."
    },
    {
      "id": "wbweben",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Direct Current (DC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j862u4s",
      "content": "Direct Current (DC) is the type of electric current that flows in only one direction. The magnitude of current may be constant or may vary slightly, but its direction does not change."
    },
    {
