    {
      "id": "tspldcr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Alternating Current (AC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a7gbl6m",
      "content": "Alternating Current (AC) is the type of electric current that periodically changes its direction and magnitude with time. AC is widely used for power distribution because it can be easily transmitted over long distances."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Direct current flows in one constant direction, whereas alternating current periodically reverses its direction at regular intervals.",
      "id": "ufqtgfm"
    },
    {
